The file is in the right source folder, but the Rojo mapping puts it where it won't run. In `default.project.json`, `src/client` maps to `ReplicatedStorage.Client`. Roblox doesn't run LocalScripts inside ReplicatedStorage, so `print("client")` never executes.

Client entrypoints need to live under `StarterPlayer/StarterPlayerScripts`, which runs once per player. Map it there:

```json
{
  "name": "arena",
  "tree": {
    "$className": "DataModel",
    "ReplicatedStorage": {
      "Shared": { "$path": "src/shared" },
      "Packages": { "$path": "Packages" }
    },
    "StarterPlayer": {
      "StarterPlayerScripts": {
        "Client": { "$path": "src/client" }
      }
    },
    "ServerScriptService": { "Server": { "$path": "src/server" } }
  }
}
```

Keep `src/client/init.client.luau` where it is. The server entrypoint at `src/server/init.server.luau` already runs from ServerScriptService, so it needs no change.

Client code should `require` shared modules from `ReplicatedStorage.Shared`, which is still replicated. Keeping `Client` under ReplicatedStorage would only be useful if other code needs to require client modules, which is uncommon.

I haven't edited the project file. Do you want me to apply this change?
